Maintenance rules:
- Status values: TODO, IN_PROGRESS, BLOCKED, DONE. Update status only with evidence; record PR/commit.
- A row moves to DONE only when its acceptance criteria are demonstrably met (command output, merged PR, observed behavior).
- Add details in issues or ADRs, not by inflating this table.
- BLOCKED rows carry their blocker in the Dependency column or a linked open decision.
- Detail files: create .agent/tasks/<ID>.md only when a task needs more than its row (evidence log, multi-line acceptance, design discussion). Link it from the Acceptance cell: "— detail: tasks/<ID>.md". Never create empty task files or the directory until the first file exists.
- Archival: when a phase closes (its last task DONE) or the index exceeds ~50 open rows, move DONE rows whose dependent rows are all DONE or archived into .agent/tasks/archive/<phase-slug-or-YYYY-MM>.md (append; never edit archived history). Move their task files into .agent/tasks/archive/ too. A row lives in exactly one of index or archive — status stays single-sourced.
-->

